@base <https://ontoboard.org/patterns/mwo-temporal-region.owl> .

<https://ontoboard.org/patterns/mwo-temporal-region.owl> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                                          dcterms:description "Represents temporal regions in BFO terms, distinguishing a zero-dimensional temporal region (an instant such as the start or end of an event) from a one-dimensional temporal region (an interval with a duration), related by occupies_temporal_region, has_first_instance and has_last_instance. Data about those regions - start date, end date, duration, frequency - is carried by specification datum individuals linked to their values with nfdicore:hasValue."^^xsd:string ;
                                                          dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
                                                          dcterms:title "Pattern 7: Temporal Region"^^xsd:string ;
                                                          rdfs:comment """Curated by OntoBoard 1.155.0, so that the pattern passes ODK's quality report with its default profile, names every term with a label, and is consistent and coherent. Changes: label added x8; term declared x4;
- header: dcterms:title \"Pattern 7: Temporal Region\" - the library's name for the pattern
- header: dcterms:description - the library's description of the pattern
- header: dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> - https://github.com/ISE-FIZKarlsruhe/mwo/blob/main/mwo.ttl
Each change is listed under \"curated\" in the pattern's metadata.json in OntoBoard's pattern library."""@en .

